  "reading": "That muddy, churned-up water is perfect for a duck (ダク) to paddle through and hunt. Picture the duck dabbling in the dirty pond, snapping up what it stirs loose from the muck. The messier and cloudier the water, the happier the duck — and that quack is your reminder that 濁 is read ダク.",
